        {"source": "spec", "quote": "The schematic does not show where board VCC is normally sourced from (no battery, regulator, or USB part appears anywhere..."}
      ],
      "impact": "The backup domain (RTC, backup registers, tamper) will not have a dedicated supply and may not retain state across power-down. If VBAT is required to be tied to VDD in this MCU family, the floating power pin is an ERC/design-margin issue; the main MCU core may still operate from VDD, but backup-domain behavior differs from a properly powered STM32 design.",
